From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HourlySword <hourlysword.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:09:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] FunKey S: the room pieces kept on the card; a weak name
 handed out again kept through the sweep

The pieces a room's floor and walls are drawn from (BitmapData.draw's leaves) are rasterized the first time they are
seen, most of a room entry on the console. Each piece rasterized is now also compressed (zlib 1) into
saves/leaves_<SWF length>.data and listed in .index (read at start into a table), and a piece needed again, in a later
room or session, is read back instead of being parsed and rasterized. Its key holds no pointer: the character's id and
kind (shapes, morphs at their ratio, static text; only the game file's own characters), the matrix, the colour
transform and the sub-pixel offset. The files belong to one build (the linker's build ID, now added with
-Wl,--build-id) and one game file, else they start afresh; off with mods and with ISAAC_NO_LEAFDISK; up to 16 MB;
pieces read back are checked (key, CRC). New pieces are written in the time left before the next tick (a queue of up
to 512 KB of pixels, 4 ms a tick at most), not during the room's entry. On the console: the same rooms again, no room
entry over 150 ms (9 without the pieces); other rooms, 25% of the pieces from the card after one session.

Weak clip names (atomOfWeak, the previous patch): the collector frees garbage over the following ticks, and the game's
names come back ("sz1" again), so a weak name found again in the intern table while still waiting to be freed was freed
under its new clip (a crash building a removed clip's target path). internWeak now marks a weak name it hands out
again while a sweep is in progress.
